# NSW MyRTA Driving Test Availability Scraper (Userscript – Debug Edition)

**This is a simple Tampermonkey / Violentmonkey userscript**  
Main purpose: **debugging and manual data collection** of NSW driving test availability from myrta.com.

**Original scraper credit goes to:**  
https://github.com/teehee567/nsw-drivers-test  
(This userscript is a simplified, browser-only version inspired by the project – no Rust/Python backend here)

### What this script does

- Runs **only on** the MyRTA booking pages after you log in, on your own client side (USE WITH CAUTION, it takes hours)
- Lets you manually start scraping available test timeslots for driving centres
- Saves result as `bookings.json` in the format roughly compatible with many NSW test monitors

### How to use (debug mode)

1. Install Tampermonkey / Violentmonkey extension
2. Create new script → paste the whole code
3. Log in to https://www.myrta.com
4. Go through the booking flow until you reach the **"Choose a location"** / centre selection page
5. You should see a red **"Start Scraper"** button top-right
6. Click it → confirm the number of centres
7. Wait… (each centre takes ~3–8 seconds depending on network)
8. When finished → browser will auto-download `bookings.json`

### What NOT tested

Other booking than the car driving test.

